<title>JAPAN: Nippon Mining to cut indium price by 5,000 yen.</title>
<headline>Nippon Mining to cut indium price by 5,000 yen.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nippon Mining and Metals Co said on Thursday it was lowering the price of indium by 5,000 yen per kg to between 35,000 yen and 40,000 yen per kg, effective from Friday.</p>
<p>The price cut is in reaction to movements in overseas markets, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Nippon Mining produces 20 to 30 tonnes of indium per year, while global production is about 130 to 150 tonnes.</p>
<p>Japan is the world's top consumer of indium, which in alloy form is used for a number of industrial purposes, including the manufacture of liquid crystal displays.</p>
</text>
